title: $:/plugins/tiddlywiki/hive-storage/readme
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

! Hive storage plugin

Stores the working copies of the tiddlers of a wiki in the IndexedDB database that is built into the browser instead of in browser local storage.

The browser local storage is limited to about 5 MB, which is not enough for larger wikis. The IndexedDB database of the browser is a much larger and more capable store, and is used here.

The plugin is part of the [[https://github.com/true-peak-org/TiddlyWiki5|Hive plugin set]] and is used by the [[hive|Hive edition]] of the TiddlyWiki5 repository.

!! Settings

|!Setting |!Default |!Description |
|Enabled |`yes` |Whether the working copies are stored in the Indexed database |
|Save filter |`[all[]] -[prefix[$:/state/popup/]] -[prefix[$:/temp/]] -[prefix[$:/HistoryList]]` |The filter that determines which tiddlers are saved |
|Quota exceeded alert | |The alert message that is shown when storing a tiddler fails |
|Indexed database persistence | |The permission state that prevents the browser from evicting the database |

! Requirements

The plugin requires a browser with support for the Indexed database API and a secure context.
